-- lib/cost.cub — the cost model for navigation, first form (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.14 “F33 — Navigation: the concrete form”, "cost model (open
-- thread)"): the score of a step is the recorded cost of its result — the machine's own step
-- count for the key at the result's head, as the store records it beside each accepted
-- definition (`ok <steps> <checker>`) — estimated by the result's size where no record exists.
-- A cost model is a value (Code → Word); navigation parameterized by one (navigate-by) is
-- lib/nav.cub's navigation with the score abstracted; nav.cub's choice is navigate-by size-cost.
-- The recorded steps are read through %gsteps (the steps checked definition n took, from this run
-- or from the store's ok line); a table given as data stands in for them where a reading wants
-- its own figures. Loaded after lib/nav.cub.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- tables and models
-- a table: a Lst of (global index , recorded steps)
cost-lookup g tbl = case tbl of lnil → none; lcons e r → (if %weq (fst e) g then some (snd e) else cost-lookup g r)
